  https://github.com/AhmetArif0/hermes-ntfy-approval
  commit 95d3a4b838073d6908c578ca1a9f04154349a2cf
  MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 AhmetArif0 (LICENSE)

cell.lisp rewrites the original ntfy-approval transport as one Nodecode cell: the ntfy
publish-with-buttons and reply-topic round trip, one random code per button, redirects not
followed, the token kept out of the notification, the topic-length floor without a token, the
withdrawal of a notification once the wait is over, and the fail-closed rule that no answer, an
unreachable server or an unset topic denies the call. The suspicious-command judgement, which
Hermes' own gate did, is this rewrite's: a rule table read against the commands an eval call
runs. The test system's fake ntfy server stands in for the wire, since the tests run offline.
Written as a Nodecode cell against the cell contract; no Python, and none of the original's
files run here.
